Subject: Cantor Instance Foundation P0

@ [specification_uuid] d7e6055f-d40e-46c4-a757-2db3b77c7108
@ [source_snapshot_uuid] 670483d0-3f70-49b5-8d7c-d924065ce004
@ [signature_protocol_uuid] ad10f10f-d506-48ef-a805-f8b0a133766c
@ [published_predecessor] 80f2ef9a8c1709e9e0dc12d70fc340a53919eec2

& [Objective]
  + define the smallest reusable Cantor instance contract that can admit SOP Eclipse and later instances without confusing instance behavior with kernel authority
  + retain an exact deterministic inventory of selected semantic candidates from the live Eclipse checkout while excluding generated mass

& [Roles]
  + [kernel] owns contract validation compatibility decisions canonical digests and authority boundaries
  + [instance] declares identity revision required capabilities provided capabilities entry points and component bindings
  + [kernel_component] implements a reusable Cantor capability and may only be admitted through an explicit kernel slot
  + [instance_adapter] binds instance-specific UI workflow or packaging without becoming kernel authority
  + [package] contributes governed semantic content without runtime or effect authority
  + [evidence] records verification without becoming executable input
  + [generated_payload] is reproducible output and is excluded from semantic-source custody

& [Requirements]
  + [CIF-001] preserve the exact user source before derived formation or implementation
  + [CIF-002] use the published commit 80f2ef9a8c1709e9e0dc12d70fc340a53919eec2 as the integration predecessor
  + [CIF-003] do not modify delete stage or normalize the live Eclipse source checkout during inventory
  + [CIF-004] inventory candidates as repository-relative sorted unique paths with exact byte count and SHA256
  + [CIF-005] distinguish tracked integration deltas governance source kernel candidates instance adapters packages evidence and generated payloads
  + [CIF-006] exclude evidence distributions workspaces worker_projects tmp target and local build state from semantic promotion by default
  + [CIF-007] define a strict machine-readable instance manifest with unknown fields refused
  + [CIF-008] bind instance identity revision kernel API profile source lineage and component identities
  + [CIF-009] declare required and provided capabilities as normalized unique identifiers
  + [CIF-010] bind every component to exactly one role and content digest
  + [CIF-011] forbid instance adapters packages and evidence from occupying kernel component slots
  + [CIF-012] forbid any instance declaration from granting itself execution provider operator or kernel authority
  + [CIF-013] compile a deterministic admitted or held compatibility result with explicit missing capabilities and refusals
  + [CIF-014] bind manifests and compatibility results with canonical SHA256 digests
  + [CIF-015] include an SOP Eclipse candidate fixture without declaring the live instance accepted
  + [CIF-016] test valid admission missing capability digest tamper duplicate identity path traversal role escalation and authority escalation
  + [CIF-017] expose a provider-free verifier CLI that performs no network process provider remote or external effect
  + [CIF-018] keep direct llama.cpp integration UI execution model invocation installation update and live initiation outside P0
  + [CIF-019] publish only owned source formation implementation tests evidence and intentional transitive manifests
  + [CIF-020] retain unresolved Eclipse artifacts as candidates instead of inferring compatibility from names or prior tests

& [Acceptance]
  + [CIF-A01] source canonical justification plan solution matrix phase lock and satisfaction signature cross-bind exactly
  + [CIF-A02] semantic custody builder and independent verifier agree on the selected live-tree inventory
  + [CIF-A03] focused debug overflow-checked release warnings-denied Clippy and format pass
  + [CIF-A04] exact workspace gates and recursive evidence pass before completion publication
  + [CIF-A05] all live process provider remote effect installation update and synthetic-trial counters remain zero

& [NonAuthority]
  + a valid instance manifest proves structural correspondence only
  + compatibility admission does not authorize execution installation provider contact model inference mutation or publication
  + semantic custody proves observed bytes at one checkpoint and does not certify their correctness or promotion eligibility
